# Office kit detail · Round 4

**Status:** Target concepts for Alex's review · **Last updated:** 2026-11-12

[Contact sheet](contact_sheet_r4.png) · [Governing brief](FEEDBACK_03.md) · [Exact prompts and 
revisions](prompts_r4.json) · [Reference board](reference_board_r4.png)

Five families, ten directions, **twenty interior views and ten small rival insets**, made with the built-in ImageGen 
tool in **10 image tries**.
Each sheet places A on the left and B on the right, hero above and play below, with a small street inset occupying 
roughly a quarter of each play panel.
Both interior cameras were requested at 1,700 mm eye height; play views use a different position from the hero.
Street insets were requested from 12,000 mm across the gap, showing three floors.
The paintings are concept references, not measured drawings or engine captures; the modelling dimensions below govern 
a build.

## Direction and the whole floor

[FEEDBACK_03.md](FEEDBACK_03.md), including its Style section, governs this pass wherever older briefs or the bible's 
general style emphasis differ.
The added Frutiger Aero influence is architectural: glossy white, rounded negative cuts, sky-filled transparency, high 
frosted inserts and soft light within a restrained blue/white/silver/navy system.
Gen X Soft Club supplies negative space, thin rules, spaced light typography and sky imagery; hard sun, deep cavities 
and room-scale cobalt retain round 3's boldness.
No greenery, bubbles, droplets, pink chrome, pastel/rainbow gradients or nostalgia props were added.

The four bible references, all three office plates, the art-bible text, the round-3 contact sheet, README and exact 
prompts were reviewed first.
The approved White Trays / Cobalt Portal paintings and the existing Unity office captures were also inspected in 
[source_review_r4.png](source_review_r4.png).
Bible references 01–03 informed the era language, 04 the massing, and the office-floor and atrium plates the open 
room, office materials, sky and depth.

**A means the round-3 pick refined for the interior**, regardless of its former letter: façade A, walls A, stair B, 
ceiling A and partition B become round-4 A.
**B means a new interior-led alternative.**
The play views bring the room-height floor index, spiral stair, cobalt carpet route and white meeting enclosure into 
the same room, with the active family leading the composition.
The stair B capsule replaces the helix on that core; it is an alternative, not a second layer over the helix.

**Proposed build mix: façade B, walls A, stair A, ceiling A, partition B.**
This keeps direct floor and route cues while using the capsule bay and high skyglass lintel to make the era visible 
throughout the office.
These are recommendations for review, not approved changes to the kit or the office decision.

## Fixed boundaries and depth convention

All dimensions below are **millimetres**.
**Recessed** means cut inward from the piece's original exposed face; **flush** means 0 mm proud.
Every new move below is recessed or flush: **new proud geometry is 0 mm throughout**, beneath the allowed 15 mm 
maximum.
White islands between carved numeral strokes remain at the original wall plane; they must never become attached, 
raised white numerals.
Likewise the helix is a groove in the core, never a ribbon projecting from it.

Keep the existing envelopes, pivots, flat snap lands, floor/soffit contacts and all colliders.
Use the existing 4,000 bay, 600 façade sill, 4,300 floor-to-soffit, 4,500 storey and 200 slab.
Service openings stay 1,200 × 2,400; the actual silver leaf remains 1,180 × 2,380 × 40 with its hinge pivot unchanged.
Façade columns remain 400 × 240 × 4,300; corner columns retain their 420 width.
Stair core / tread / rail / cage radii remain 800 / 2,600 / 2,630 / 2,750.
The full-height red stair leaf stays 1,750 × 4,200 × 200, with the existing hardware allowance retained.

Partition runs remain 4,000 / 2,000 × 100 deep × 2,500 high, leaving **1,800 open air above** to the office ceiling.
No roof or raised room floor is part of either partition direction.
All partition glass from 450 to 2,100 stays near-clear and unobstructed; opaque/diffuse upper treatments start at 
2,100 or higher.
The lower frame is a narrow vertical band at the pane footprint, never a platform below the room.

The existing [glass specification](../../../../docs/systems/GLASS.md) remains authoritative: one broad and one thin 
translucent diagonal streak, no actual mirror reflection.
Sky sheen and gloss are visual proposals concentrated at grazing angles and on opaque finishes; the clear transmission 
region must still reveal dark suits through two panes.
High frosted glass in partition B is a separate proposed material, not a replacement for the clear gameplay panes.
Keep the original colliders over the original bounds: these reliefs do not add cover, change the walking surface or 
change any collision outcome.
Do not combine opposing recesses through a thin piece; preserve the minimum skins listed below and the original 
snap/contact lands.

## 01 · Inner façade

[Sheet](01_Facade/sheet_r4.png) · **2 image tries**

**A — Folded inner piers rake sunlight across the office route.**

- **Pieces:** `Column_Facade`, `Column_CornerL/R`, the inner head and sill finishes of `Window_4m/2m`.
- **Pier:** relocate the round-3 folded pocket to the inner face: **recessed 160**, 280-wide cobalt back, from height 
660 to 4,160, retaining 20 side lands and the 140 head land; inner transition radius 40 is cut inward.
- **Opposite face:** keep this variant's street face at its original outer plane, **flush 0**; do not retain an 
opposing 160 street pocket, leaving 80 back skin behind the inner cut.
- **Head:** a selected 100-high field at 4,200–4,300 is **recessed 60**, with cobalt continuing from the inner pier; 
contact lands remain untouched.
- **Sill:** inner tray 120 high is **recessed 40**, below the unchanged 600 top; where it overlaps the existing 
120-deep street tray, keep 40 skin within the 200 sill.
- **Silver edge:** **recessed 2**, with the white satin/gloss finish **flush 0**; neither becomes a projecting fin or 
bench.
- **2001-future cue:** a sharp folded white shell paired with a radiused inner cut, consumer-tech gloss and a 
precisely inset silver edge gives the window bay a designed-product character beyond a 2025 office mullion.
- **Play read:** the existing sill remains low cover; piers rhythmically frame long views, and raking sun carries 
their form onto the route.

**B — Capsule-cut sky bays turn the window line into an air terminal.**

- **Pieces:** the same columns and inner window finishes, with the original pane planes and rectangular openings 
retained.
- **Pier capsule:** 180 wide × 3,400 high, end radius 90, **recessed 90** into the inner face; retain 150 back skin 
and a **flush 0** street face without the old opposing deep pocket.
- **Inner corner:** radius 80 is carved inward within the 400 × 240 pier, with maximum inward removal 80; no rounded 
tube is attached outside it.
- **Head cove:** 100 high at 4,200–4,300, **recessed 65**, with a 10-wide light line at the recessed back, never proud 
of the head.
- **Sill:** 120-high, radius-40 inner concavity is **recessed 40**, retaining the same 600 top and 40 minimum skin 
where the street tray overlaps.
- **Type and finish:** department codes are printed **flush 0**; silver edges are **recessed 2**, gloss finish **flush 
0**.
- **2001-future cue:** tall capsule cavities, softly sky-lit gloss and spaced department labels recall optimistic 
air-terminal/product design rather than a present-day curtain wall.
- **Play read:** rounded inner relief changes the light while leaving the crossing lane, sill cover and window 
sightline intact.

**Materials:** existing `Wall_PaperWhite`, `Accent_Cobalt`, `Trim_Navy`, `Glass_Clear`; proposals `Finish_WhiteGloss`, 
`Metal_BrushedSilver`, and B's `Light_CoveWhite` with a thin cyan accent.
**Build B:** its inner capsules carry the requested era language into every window-side play view without designing a 
new exterior façade.

## 02 · Walls and door

[Sheet](02_Walls_Door/sheet_r4.png) · **3 image tries**

**A — A recessed floor index folds into a polished corporate spine.**

- **Pieces:** `Wall_Solid_*`, adjacent `Wall_Door_4m` visual finishes, room-set floor-code composition and `Door_Leaf` 
handle finish.
- **Index:** 4,200 high × approximately 3,600 wide, 50 clear above/below, numeral-shaped blue-backed strokes 
**recessed 120** in the 200 wall, leaving 80 skin; the white face and counters stay **flush 0**.
- **Corners:** radius-120 glyph turns are cut inward to the same 120 maximum depth; the composition wraps the existing 
wall corner without moving its envelope.
- **Door surround:** 30-wide reveal **recessed 15**, outer corner radius 60 cut inward, while the actual 1,200 × 2,400 
opening stays rectangular.
- **Leaf:** existing 40 thickness unchanged; handle cup **recessed 12**, silver leaf finish **flush 0**.
- **Graphics:** thin department code and hairline rule printed **flush 0**; gloss finish **flush 0**.
- **2001-future cue:** room-sized radiused negative lettering in a polished white shell, very light spaced corporate 
type and inset silver feel like a speculative corporate identity system rather than applied contemporary office 
signage.
- **Play read:** the number identifies the floor and core from a crossing position; the ordinary service door remains 
subordinate and readable.

**B — A carved sky-lens portal makes the service core an airport landmark.**

- **Pieces:** `Wall_Solid_*_Cobalt`, the fixed `Wall_Door_4m` surround/portal-head finish and its existing wall 
return; moving leaf remains unchanged.
- **Portal:** rounded-rectangle annular pocket 3,600 wide × 4,000 high, 500-wide band, outer radius 400, **recessed 
100** in the 200 wall, retaining 100 skin.
- **Inner bowl:** radius-70 concave transition is carved within that 100 recess; white lands remain **flush 0**, never 
a raised ring.
- **Sky insert:** 2,200 × 800 printed sky panel on the solid upper wall, face **recessed 20**, silver edge **recessed 
2**; this is a graphic, not another window or an opening through the wall.
- **Door:** original opening, leaf and pivot unchanged; leaf finish **flush 0**, existing handle cup **recessed 12** 
as in A.
- **Type:** department label and fine grid printed **flush 0**; any high cyan accent sits at the recessed cove back, 
not proud.
- **2001-future cue:** a huge rounded negative surround, a framed sky image and sparse legal microtype evoke a 
multinational's airport-lounge vision of the future rather than today's plain service portal.
- **Play read:** the capsule perimeter draws the eye to the existing entry; the supporting floor index stays visible 
on another spine face.

**Materials:** existing white, cobalt, navy and `Door_Leaf`; proposals `Finish_WhiteGloss`, `Metal_BrushedSilver`, B's 
`Graphic_SkyPrint` and a restrained `Light_CoveWhite` accent.
**Build A:** a floor-sized index communicates location more directly and keeps the room's other curved moves from 
competing with another portal.

## 03 · Stair

[Sheet](03_Stair/sheet_r4.png) · **1 image try**

**A — The cobalt helix is cut into a glossy white stair core.**

- **Pieces:** visual surface of `Stair_Column`; existing `Stair_Steps`, handrail, cage, flight collider and locked 
leaf retained.
- **Helix:** 1,000-high channel, one turn per 4,500 rise, **recessed 160 radially**, from original radius 800 to blue 
back radius 640.
- **Edge:** 40-radius inner bevel cut within that recess; white lands remain at the original radius, **flush 0**, with 
original top/bottom contact lands retained and phase aligned across storeys.
- **Finish:** gloss white shell and satin cobalt back **flush 0** relative to their respective modelled surfaces; no 
external ribbon, new tread lip or cage band.
- **Red leaf:** original full-height 1,750 × 4,200 × 200 envelope and hardware retained; small lock mark printed 
**flush 0**, no added raised lock plate.
- **2001-future cue:** the glossy white cylindrical shell and deeply inlaid blue spiral combine early 
consumer-electronics finish with optimistic transport architecture; the silver open stair stays functional.
- **Play read:** the continuous twist signals upward movement from across the floor without screening the walking 
annulus.

**B — A capsule landing niche makes each floor a calm arrival point.**

- **Pieces:** alternative visual surface of `Stair_Column`; other stair pieces as A.
- **Niche:** 1,000 wide × 3,000 high, end radius 500, from height 750 to 3,750, **recessed 120 radially** into the 
approach face, blue back radius 680.
- **Edge:** radius-50 concave transition carved within the 120 recess; silver inner edge **recessed 2** from its 
surrounding white face.
- **Code:** floor number and UP indicator printed **flush 0** on the niche back; the 10-wide status line is at that 
same **recessed 120** back plane.
- **Red leaf:** retained full height, lock mark **flush 0** as A; no second helix is combined with the capsule 
treatment.
- **2001-future cue:** a tall cobalt capsule set into a glossy white landing column, with light typography and a tiny 
status line, reads as a turn-of-the-millennium arrival terminal rather than a modern freestanding digital sign.
- **Play read:** a stable landing code faces the approach while the existing visible treads explain upward progression.

**Materials:** existing `Wall_PaperWhite`, `Accent_Cobalt`, `Stair_Aluminium`, `Trim_Navy`, `Door_LockedRed`, 
`Glass_Clear`; proposals `Finish_WhiteGloss`, B's `Metal_BrushedSilver` and a tiny `Light_CoveWhite` status accent.
**Build A:** the spiral remains the stronger shared landmark and communicates upward movement without needing to read 
text.

## 04 · Ceiling and floor

[Sheet](04_Ceiling_Floor/sheet_r4.png) · **2 image tries**

**A — A flush cobalt route runs beneath a capsule-cut light cove.**

- **Pieces:** floor finish and underside of `Slab_*`, the approach in `Slab_Stairwell`, existing spine return, 
recessed visual variant of `Ceiling_LightStrip`.
- **Carpet:** 2,000-wide route made from four 500 rows, including radiused material turns, **flush 0**, without steps 
or changes to the slab top.
- **Cove:** 2,000-wide capsule-ended plan, end radius 1,000, **recessed 120 upward** from soffit 4,300 to back 4,420; 
80 slab skin remains.
- **Inner edge:** radius 60 carved within the 120 cut; white lands stay at the original soffit, **flush 0**, not a 
dropped surround.
- **Light:** 10-wide rear line at **recessed 120**; its soft white/cyan lighting gradient adds no geometry.
- **Wall return:** existing 4,000 × 4,300 face with route colour continuing onto it and a **recessed 120** return; no 
added partition or raised wall skin.
- **Tile field:** original 500 grid remains **flush 0** outside the pocket.
- **2001-future cue:** the capsule-ended negative cove, glossy moulded edge and gently luminous white line above a 
matte cobalt route suggest a brand-managed 2001 transport interior rather than modern exposed-services lighting.
- **Play read:** carpet and overhead negative space agree on the approach to the visible stair entrance.

**B — Shallow sky lenses open the ceiling above a carpet island.**

- **Pieces:** slab underside and carpet finish as A; no new skylight or structural hole.
- **Lenses:** two elliptical pockets, each 3,000 × 2,000 in plan, **recessed 140 upward** to back 4,440 in the same 
200 slab, retaining 60 skin.
- **Edges:** radius-60 concave cuts within the 140 maximum; all outer white lands remain at soffit 4,300, **flush 0**, 
never suspended rings.
- **Sky:** a flat printed acoustic insert at one lens back, **recessed 140**; the other back remains white at the same 
depth, with one restrained cove line there.
- **Carpet island:** 4,000 × 2,400 elliptical material zone and the smaller link toward the stair are **flush 0** in 
the 500-tile field; grey circulation lanes pass beside it.
- **2001-future cue:** shallow ovals containing idealised sky imagery, translucent-looking light and vast white space 
are the strongest Soft Club / architectural Aero move in this family, unlike a current office coffer.
- **Play read:** the island identifies a pause/meeting zone while leaving an obvious open route and cross-window 
visibility around it.

**Materials:** existing `Ceiling_Tile`, `Floor_Carpet`, white, cobalt and navy; proposals `Floor_Carpet_Cobalt`, 
`Finish_WhiteGloss`, `Light_CoveWhite`, B's `Graphic_SkyPrint` on an acoustic finish.
**Build A:** it strengthens navigation using the existing approach; B is the bolder sky-ceiling alternative if 
atmosphere takes priority over the single continuous route.

## 05 · Glass partition

[Sheet](05_Partition/sheet_r4.png) · **2 image tries**

**A — A carved white meeting box reveals a cobalt interior.**

- **Pieces:** visual upper/base finishes of `Partition_Glass_4m/2m`, butt-jointed corner, existing rear 
`Wall_Solid_4m_Cobalt` face.
- **Header:** 400 high at 2,100–2,500, maximum 100 depth; folded diagonal cavity **recessed 70**, retaining 30 skin, 
with radius-60 inward end transitions within that depth.
- **Base:** 450-high vertical frame, only 100 deep, **recessed 60**, retaining 40 skin; its top is a narrow ledge, 
never a floor deck.
- **Rear wall:** existing 4,000 × 4,300 cobalt face with return **recessed 120**, retaining 80 skin in the 200 wall; 
it is separate from the low clear partition.
- **Silver edge:** **recessed 2**, gloss finish **flush 0**; the clear pane plane remains **flush 0** relative to its 
original placement.
- **2001-future cue:** the sharply carved yet gently radiused glossy-white frame and clean silver joints make the 
meeting enclosure feel like speculative product architecture rather than a standard 2025 office glass box.
- **Play read:** the frame declares a room while its low height, open air above and clear standing region preserve 
views through it.

**B — A translucent sky lintel floats above an entirely clear room.**

- **Pieces:** same partition and rear wall pieces, with the same original pane and flat snap planes.
- **High capsule:** 3,000 long × 300 high, end radius 150, wholly in the 2,100–2,500 upper band, **recessed 65** into 
the 100 envelope, retaining 35 back skin.
- **Frosted insert:** face **recessed 30** from the original front; diffusion and soft cyan-to-white are confined to 
this high insert, never the 450–2,100 clear region.
- **Silver edge:** **recessed 2**; high room code and hairline printed **flush 0 relative to the insert**, therefore 
30 behind the original frame plane.
- **Corner:** radius-60 inner frame fillet cut inward, maximum inward removal 60 within the original 100 depth; no new 
curved wall/pane outside the original envelope.
- **Base:** 250-high white vertical band, 100 deep, **recessed 40**, retaining 60 skin; carpet level unchanged, 
**flush 0**.
- **Rear wall:** same existing cobalt face and **recessed 120** return as A; dark figures use a pale side background 
for contrast.
- **2001-future cue:** pale translucent skyglass above a completely clear room, capsule ends, inset silver and tiny 
light corporate type directly express the turn-of-the-millennium Soft Club / Aero brief without resorting to greenery 
or nostalgic props.
- **Play read:** the high lintel identifies the room while the entire standing sightline stays transparent and the 
crossing lane stays open.

**Materials:** existing white, cobalt, navy and `Glass_Clear`; proposals `Finish_WhiteGloss`, `Metal_BrushedSilver`, 
B's `Glass_FrostedHigh`.
**Build B:** the high frosted lintel adds the requested period character where it can remain outside the critical 
standing sightline.

## Material proposals, not new approved assets

| Proposed name | Intended surface and role |
| --- | --- |
| `Finish_WhiteGloss` | Paper White satin/gloss finish on the specified carved opaque surfaces; shader/material 
variation, not added mesh thickness. |
| `Metal_BrushedSilver` | Quiet brushed silver on the specified inset edges; reuse existing aluminium where it 
produces the intended result. |
| `Light_CoveWhite` | Restrained white cove light with a single thin cyan accent; no neon strip network or broad cyan 
architecture. |
| `Floor_Carpet_Cobalt` | Same low-noise 500 carpet tile scale, cobalt route/island at exactly the existing floor 
level. |
| `Graphic_SkyPrint` | Blue-sky photography on a recessed solid wall or acoustic ceiling insert; no added sightline 
opening. |
| `Glass_FrostedHigh` | Translucent pale sky/cyan-to-white insert only above 2,100; never assigned to clear gameplay 
panes. |

The paintings depict material and lighting intent; no shader reflection system, texture, mesh, material asset or 
collider was implemented.
The current system documents therefore need no behaviour/setup update for this concept-only pass.

