@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+{
+  "tool": "Built-in image_gen.imagegen",
+  "brief": "FEEDBACK_05.md; FEEDBACK_04.md style only",
+  "reference_roles": "bible_ref_02 and bible_ref_03: era/graphic restraint; suit_reference: character proportions and 
cel style; contact_sheet_r4: capsule/sky-lens form vocabulary only, prior layout superseded",
+  "references": [
+    "C:/Users/alexf/Documents/GitHub/Seal-The-Deal/ArtSource/Kit/concepts/Office/refs/bible_ref_02.png",
+    "C:/Users/alexf/Documents/GitHub/Seal-The-Deal/ArtSource/Kit/concepts/Office/refs/bible_ref_03.png",
+    "C:/Users/alexf/Documents/GitHub/Seal-The-Deal/ArtSource/Kit/concepts/Office/refs/suit_reference.png",
+    "C:/Users/alexf/Documents/GitHub/Seal-The-Deal/ArtSource/Kit/concepts/Kit_Detail/contact_sheet_r4.png"
+  ],
+  "tries": 6,
+  "attempts": [
+    {
+      "family": "01_Corridors",
+      "attempt": 1,
+      "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: FOUR-PANEL ENVIRONMENT CONCEPT IMAGE for the game Close the 
Deal, round 5. Make a wide 3:2 image at highest resolution available, ideally 3072x2048. Exact layout: seamless four 
equally sized landscape views in a 2-column x 2-row grid; tiny straight white central gutters; no title, no captions, 
no diagrams, no border text. LEFT COLUMN direction A, RIGHT COLUMN direction B. TOP ROW HERO, BOTTOM ROW PLAY. Each of 
the four views is a distinct first-person eye-level composition with camera 1.7 metres above the local floor, level 
horizon, 65-degree horizontal field of view. Bottom views must use a different camera position, show close foreground 
cover, an approaching corner or doorway, and an angular dark-suited enemy partially visible THROUGH near-clear glass, 
with crisp cel shadows. No weapon/HUD overlay. Design one massive INTERIOR office labyrinth for fast close quarters 
movement combat: tight branching routes that rejoin, short controlled sightlines, occasional wide hub, never a 
twin-tower sniper office. Mostly interior, sky visible only in a deliberate window or printed sky insert. No 
street/exterior inset.\nSTYLE: clearly STYLIZED IN-GAME SCREENSHOT, clean deliberately simplified geometry and hard 
designed shadow masses, sharp cel-shaded elongated angular lawyer characters, glossy abstract corporate future 
imagined in 2001, optimistic product architecture, Gen X Soft Club restraint, architectural Frutiger Aero WITHOUT 
bubbles. High-gloss paper-white lacquer, polished pale resin floor with soft blurred reflections of light and dark 
figures, glossy storey-height cobalt blocks, silver inset edges, near-clear glass with ONLY one broad and one thin 
translucent diagonal sheen per pane. Shiny but simple material response, no photoreal textures, no archviz photo, no 
realistic lens/DOF. Blue-white-silver-navy palette; cyan only ONE narrow 10 mm route line. Flat clean ceilings with 
long recessed white coves; capsule cuts, curved negative spaces and sky-lens motifs. Clear glass is second main 
material after white; dark enemy stays readable through two panes. Frost ONLY above 2.1 m or below 0.45 m. No opaque 
bars from knee to head across standing figures. No mirror glass, no carpet, no ceiling tile grid, no 
printers/monitors/filing clutter, no plants, no grime, no pipes/greeble, no neon cyberpunk, no purple/pink/rainbow 
gradients, no bubbles.\nMODULARITY: 4 m and 2 m architectural grid, 4.3 m floor-to-soffit, 200 mm walls/slabs, 
standard rectangular door openings 1.2 m wide x 2.4 m high; larger open corridor mouths are 2 or 4 m, not enlarged 
doors. Structural volumes stay rectilinear at snap edges; curves are inward cuts INSIDE wall bounds. All detail flush 
or recessed, nothing projecting outside source wall plane. No giant attached rings. Big zone lettering is flush 
printed/inlaid, no raised numerals. Keep white standing-height backgrounds behind enemies. The references supply style 
and character proportions ONLY: strip out their carpets, office clutter, street scenes, floor 32, rival towers and 
