+# Office labyrinth kit detail · Round 5
+
+**Status:** Target concepts for Alex's review · **Last updated:** 2026-11-12
+
+[Contact sheet](contact_sheet_r5.png) · [Governing brief](FEEDBACK_05.md) · [Style notes](FEEDBACK_04.md) · [Exact 
prompts](prompts_r5.json)
+
+Five families, ten directions, **20 interior views and five top-down sketches**, made with the built-in 
**image_gen.imagegen** tool in **six image tries**.
+
+Each family sheet puts **A left / B right, hero above / play below**, with a one-line caption per direction and a 
shared route sketch underneath.
+All cameras were requested at **1,700 mm above their local walking surface**.
+Atrium A's play camera is on the mezzanine; the other play cameras are on the lower floor.
+These are generated concept paintings, not engine captures or measured drawings; the proposed dimensions below govern 
a build.
+
+## Direction and source review
+
+[FEEDBACK_05.md](FEEDBACK_05.md) governs layout and supersession; FEEDBACK_04 supplies the retained glossy, 
glass-heavy, abstract style.
+The game is one interior office labyrinth with short combat loops, readable corners, branching routes and quick 
vertical links.
+STRAFTAT informs pacing/map flow only through the brief; no layout or visual asset was copied.
+
+The round-4 contact sheet and complete README were reviewed before generation, along with the art-bible text, **all 
four bible references, all three office plates, the floor-plan sketch and suit reference**.
+Bible references 01–03 inform negative space, sky inserts and graphic restraint; 04 informs large white/cobalt masses.
+The office plates inform materials, glass and scale; their carpet, clutter, open tower floor plates and cross-street 
composition are superseded.
+The suit reference informs angular silhouettes, long limbs and restrained cel shadows.
+
+**A** develops round 4's capsules, sky lenses, curved glass and high frosted strips into glossy game space.
+**B** reduces each family to abstract planes or masses with enough office identity, cover and navigation to play.
+There are no street insets, rival towers, repeated floor 32, repeated red doors or repeated helixes.
+
+**Suggested build mix: corridors A / junctions B / rooms A / atrium B / glass B.**
+This is a recommendation for review, not approval or implementation of a new kit.
+
+## Shared build boundaries
+
+Dimensions below are **millimetres** unless explicitly marked metres.
+Sketch distances are **proposed layout targets**, not observed gameplay measurements.
+Each sketch describes topology and approximate placement; A/B variants share the route diagram rather than matching 
every painted camera exactly.
+
+- Keep the **4,000 / 2,000 grid**, front-left floor-level wall/slab pivots, thickness toward local −Z, flat snap 
faces and 90-degree assembly turns.
+- Keep existing walls **200 thick**, soffit **4,300**, storey **4,500**, slab **200**.
+- Keep ordinary doors **1,200 × 2,400** and the **1,180 × 2,380 × 40** leaf with its hinge pivot.
+- Open **2,000 or 4,000 corridor mouths** omit wall modules; they are not widened doors.
+- Keep flat partitions **4,000 / 2,000 × 100 deep × 2,500 high**, with **1,800 open air above**.
+- Keep spiral core / tread / handrail-path / cage radii **800 / 2,600 / 2,630 / 2,750** and centre pivot.
+- Keep window bounds and **600 sill** at selected outer routes; windows no longer determine the whole floor plan.
+
+**All proposed applied detail is flush or recessed: new proud detail is 0 mm**, below the 15 mm maximum.
+Flush means the original exposed plane; recessed means inward from it.
+A cover block's stated size is its whole proposed envelope, not a 15 mm wall detail.
+Preserve flat snap/contact lands and the remaining skins listed below; do not combine opposing cuts through a thin 
piece.
+
+Large rounded corners require a **proposed 2,000 × 2,000 return module**, carved inside its grid-cell bounds, with 
flat end lands and the same floor-level pivot convention.
+A curved-glass return also needs a new 2 × 2 m cell with flat end connections; do not bend it out of an existing 
100-deep flat panel's envelope.
+Existing 4 m/2 m flat pieces retain their bounds.
+Clear route widths must be maintained after placing new returns, cover or guards.
+
+**Height exception proposed only for family 04:** omit the middle slab over the atrium void, retain the upper deck at 
**4,500**, and retain its normal soffit at **8,800 above the lower floor**.
+Adjacent rooms and occupied areas beneath the mezzanine still have **4,300 clear**.
+There is no half-storey underneath a normal 4.3 m ceiling, and no new ordinary door size is proposed.
+
+## Material proposals
+
+These are later build targets, not approved material assets or shader work.
+
+| Finish | Proposal |
+| --- | --- |
+| Gloss white lacquer | Paper White #F3F4F4; smoothness about **0.90**, non-metallic, clean broad highlights. |
+| Gloss cobalt | Corporate Cobalt #244FB9; smoothness about **0.94**; full-height fields/returns, with pale backing 
behind enemies. |
+| Polished pale resin | Pale blue-grey/white; smoothness **0.92–0.97**; flush cobalt inlays; softly blurred 
architecture/figure reflections as visual targets. |
+| Inset silver | Smoothness about **0.72**, quiet joints/treads; no opaque bars across players. |
+| Clear glass | Near-clear tint, approximately **0.05 base alpha**; one broad and one thin translucent diagonal 
streak; pale grazing edge; **no mirror image**. |
+| Frosted glass | Separate diffuse header **2,100–2,500** or base below **450**; proposed low band stops at **350**. |
+| Light/sky | Recessed white coves, cyan only a **10-wide** inlay, restrained bloom; flat sky prints above combat 
height. |
+
+Glass follows the supplied [glass specification](../../../../docs/systems/GLASS.md).
+Keep the **450–2,100** region unobstructed and figures readable through **two panes**.
+A frosted header identifies a boundary; it is not full-body concealment or hard cover.
+An intact pane shows enemies but blocks the walking route; a **cleared break opening** has no pane or continuous 
threshold rail.
+The paintings do not determine first-shot penetration, shots-to-break or debris lifetime; those belong to the 
shooting lane.
+
+The current Unity material still named **Floor_Carpet** already has no base texture, colour **#B8C2CE** and 
smoothness **0.97**.
+That historical name is an import mapping, not evidence that the live material is carpet.
+Current baked floor probes omit moving players, so painted figure reflections remain an **explicit visual proposal**.
+Reuse the polished floor as a starting point; this pass adds no reflection system.
+
+## 01 · Corridors
+
+[Sheet](01_Corridors/sheet_r5.png) · [Top-down](01_Corridors/layout_r5.png) · **1 image try**
+
+### A — Capsule loop
+
+**Idea:** a capsule-lit corner and tall cobalt niche make the next turn recognisable.
+
+- **Kit:** existing Slab_*, Wall_Solid_4m/2m, cobalt variants, Partition_Glass_4m/2m and selected Window_4m/2m; 
proposed RoundedReturn_2x2, curved-glass return, capsule cove and low counter.
+- **Form:** niche **600 × 3,400**, end radius **300**, **recessed 60** in a 200 wall, leaving **140 skin**; silver 
**recessed 2**; sky print **recessed 20** above **2,600**; cove **recessed 80** in the slab, leaving **120 skin**; 
floor colour **flush 0**; cyan **10 wide**, **recessed 2**, filled flush.
+- **Materials:** gloss white/cobalt, polished resin, clear glass with high frost, inset silver and printed sky.
+- **Play:** **16 × 12 m section**, **4 m main route / 2 m open bypass**, reconnecting around the island; **4–8 m 
target exposed views**; **1.1 m counter** outside circulation; full-height returns stop the next sightline.
+- **Navigate/read:** **L / LEGAL capsule**, cobalt floor field and thin guide turning toward the hub; white backing 
preserves the glass-side enemy silhouette.
+
+### B — Offset planes
+
+**Idea:** staggered planes make the turn itself the landmark.
+
+- **Kit:** the same flat slabs/walls/partitions; proposed low block counter and flush L graphic; no curved-return 
mesh.
+- **Form:** stagger returns **2,000** on the grid; L/colour **flush 0**; silver **recessed 2**; ceiling slot 
**recessed 40**, leaving **160 slab skin**; cyan as A; no fins or raised letters.
+- **Materials:** glossy planar white/cobalt, resin, near-clear glass and separate high frost.
+- **Play:** shared loop and **2 m branch**, **4–8 m views**, **1.1 m counter** and full-height returns; offsets 
prevent a single uninterrupted tunnel.
+- **Navigate/read:** storey-height flush **L**, asymmetrical returns and an open branch; keep the enemy's slot 
against white.
+
+**Build A:** its capsule corner carries the era and the route without requiring small text.
+B supplies the cheaper flat-wall connector.
