+## Existing kit items to reconsider
+
+These are handoff flags, not changes made to the kit.
+
+| Existing item/assumption | Labyrinth handoff |
+| --- | --- |
+| Rival façade, street trays, three-floor exterior composition | Selected outer window routes replace the mandatory 
street read; exterior detailing no longer leads this kit. |
+| Carpet/tiled-ceiling source language | Unity's floor is already polished, but the kit README/source texture 
workflow still describe carpet and ceiling tiles; retain polished mapping and propose flat coved ceilings. |
+| One portal/floor index per tower floor | Zones need distinct landmarks; L/R/C/H/A are proposed department 
identities, not a new global numbering rule. |
+| Frame-wide partition collider | The source builder places collision over the whole partition on its frame; the 
shooting lane must coordinate pane, frame/threshold and collision removal for a walkable break opening. |
+| Fixed stair cage/silver handrail | The colliding cage and opaque rail need review for transparent combat guards; 
this pass does not decide destructibility or collision policy. |
+| Full-height locked red stair leaf | It belongs to earlier progression gating and can obstruct fast loops; this pass 
neither assumes it on every combat stair nor removes its game rule. |
+| Spiral as sole vertical link | The 1.8 m radial annulus is less direct than the proposed main stair; wide stairs, 
mezzanine edges, ramp and drop remain proposed modules. |
+| 600-high window sill | Keep at outer windows; it is below the requested 1.0–1.2 m crouch-cover range and cannot be 
the sole interior cover piece. |
+| No dedicated clean low-cover family | 1.1 m capsule/block counters need explicit meshes/colliders; open-legged 
desks do not provide the painted cover. |
+| Baked floor reflections | Moving figures are omitted currently; painted figure reflections are a target, not an 
implemented effect/performance claim. |
+
+The kit README's tower layout/projectile assumptions are older than FEEDBACK_05.
+**FEEDBACK_05 is authoritative for these concepts**; projectile interaction stays with the shooting lane.
+No gameplay, model, prefab, collider, material, shader or netcode implementation was changed.
+No system setup changes were made, and the write-only-here instruction excludes updates to boards/system docs 
elsewhere.
