+# Office labyrinth kit detail · Round 5
+
+**Status:** Target concepts for Alex's review · **Last updated:** 2026-11-12
+
+[Contact sheet](contact_sheet_r5.png) · [Governing brief](FEEDBACK_05.md) · [Style notes](FEEDBACK_04.md) · [Exact 
prompts](prompts_r5.json)
+
+Five families, ten directions, **20 interior views and five top-down sketches**, made with the built-in 
**image_gen.imagegen** tool in **six image tries**.
+
+Each family sheet puts **A left / B right, hero above / play below**, with a one-line caption per direction and a 
shared route sketch underneath.
+All cameras were requested at **1,700 mm above their local walking surface**.
+Atrium A's play camera is on the mezzanine; the other play cameras are on the lower floor.
+These are generated concept paintings, not engine captures or measured drawings; the proposed dimensions below govern 
a build.
+
+## Direction and source review
+
+[FEEDBACK_05.md](FEEDBACK_05.md) governs layout and supersession; FEEDBACK_04 supplies the retained glossy, 
glass-heavy, abstract style.
+The game is one interior office labyrinth with short combat loops, readable corners, branching routes and quick 
vertical links.
+STRAFTAT informs pacing/map flow only through the brief; no layout or visual asset was copied.
+
+The round-4 contact sheet and complete README were reviewed before generation, along with the art-bible text, **all 
four bible references, all three office plates, the floor-plan sketch and suit reference**.
+Bible references 01–03 inform negative space, sky inserts and graphic restraint; 04 informs large white/cobalt masses.
+The office plates inform materials, glass and scale; their carpet, clutter, open tower floor plates and cross-street 
composition are superseded.
+The suit reference informs angular silhouettes, long limbs and restrained cel shadows.
+
+**A** develops round 4's capsules, sky lenses, curved glass and high frosted strips into glossy game space.
+**B** reduces each family to abstract planes or masses with enough office identity, cover and navigation to play.
+There are no street insets, rival towers, repeated floor 32, repeated red doors or repeated helixes.
+
+**Suggested build mix: corridors A / junctions B / rooms A / atrium B / glass B.**
+This is a recommendation for review, not approval or implementation of a new kit.
+
+## Shared build boundaries
+
+Dimensions below are **millimetres** unless explicitly marked metres.
+Sketch distances are **proposed layout targets**, not observed gameplay measurements.
+Each sketch describes topology and approximate placement; A/B variants share the route diagram rather than matching 
every painted camera exactly.
+
+- Keep the **4,000 / 2,000 grid**, front-left floor-level wall/slab pivots, thickness toward local −Z, flat snap 
faces and 90-degree assembly turns.
+- Keep existing walls **200 thick**, soffit **4,300**, storey **4,500**, slab **200**.
+- Keep ordinary doors **1,200 × 2,400** and the **1,180 × 2,380 × 40** leaf with its hinge pivot.
+- Open **2,000 or 4,000 corridor mouths** omit wall modules; they are not widened doors.
+- Keep flat partitions **4,000 / 2,000 × 100 deep × 2,500 high**, with **1,800 open air above**.
+- Keep spiral core / tread / handrail-path / cage radii **800 / 2,600 / 2,630 / 2,750** and centre pivot.
+- Keep window bounds and **600 sill** at selected outer routes; windows no longer determine the whole floor plan.
+
+**All proposed applied detail is flush or recessed: new proud detail is 0 mm**, below the 15 mm maximum.
+Flush means the original exposed plane; recessed means inward from it.
+A cover block's stated size is its whole proposed envelope, not a 15 mm wall detail.
+Preserve flat snap/contact lands and the remaining skins listed below; do not combine opposing cuts through a thin 
piece.
+
+Large rounded corners require a **proposed 2,000 × 2,000 return module**, carved inside its grid-cell bounds, with 
flat end lands and the same floor-level pivot convention.
+A curved-glass return also needs a new 2 × 2 m cell with flat end connections; do not bend it out of an existing 
100-deep flat panel's envelope.
+Existing 4 m/2 m flat pieces retain their bounds.
+Clear route widths must be maintained after placing new returns, cover or guards.
+
+**Height exception proposed only for family 04:** omit the middle slab over the atrium void, retain the upper deck at 
**4,500**, and retain its normal soffit at **8,800 above the lower floor**.
+Adjacent rooms and occupied areas beneath the mezzanine still have **4,300 clear**.
+There is no half-storey underneath a normal 4.3 m ceiling, and no new ordinary door size is proposed.
+
+## Material proposals
+
+These are later build targets, not approved material assets or shader work.
+
+| Finish | Proposal |
+| --- | --- |
+| Gloss white lacquer | Paper White #F3F4F4; smoothness about **0.90**, non-metallic, clean broad highlights. |
+| Gloss cobalt | Corporate Cobalt #244FB9; smoothness about **0.94**; full-height fields/returns, with pale backing 
behind enemies. |
+| Polished pale resin | Pale blue-grey/white; smoothness **0.92–0.97**; flush cobalt inlays; softly blurred 
architecture/figure reflections as visual targets. |
+| Inset silver | Smoothness about **0.72**, quiet joints/treads; no opaque bars across players. |
+| Clear glass | Near-clear tint, approximately **0.05 base alpha**; one broad and one thin translucent diagonal 
streak; pale grazing edge; **no mirror image**. |
+| Frosted glass | Separate diffuse header **2,100–2,500** or base below **450**; proposed low band stops at **350**. |
+| Light/sky | Recessed white coves, cyan only a **10-wide** inlay, restrained bloom; flat sky prints above combat 
height. |
+
+Glass follows the supplied [glass specification](../../../../docs/systems/GLASS.md).
+Keep the **450–2,100** region unobstructed and figures readable through **two panes**.
+A frosted header identifies a boundary; it is not full-body concealment or hard cover.
+An intact pane shows enemies but blocks the walking route; a **cleared break opening** has no pane or continuous 
threshold rail.
+The paintings do not determine first-shot penetration, shots-to-break or debris lifetime; those belong to the 
shooting lane.
+
+The current Unity material still named **Floor_Carpet** already has no base texture, colour **#B8C2CE** and 
smoothness **0.97**.
+That historical name is an import mapping, not evidence that the live material is carpet.
+Current baked floor probes omit moving players, so painted figure reflections remain an **explicit visual proposal**.
+Reuse the polished floor as a starting point; this pass adds no reflection system.
+
+## 01 · Corridors
+
+[Sheet](01_Corridors/sheet_r5.png) · [Top-down](01_Corridors/layout_r5.png) · **1 image try**
+
+### A — Capsule loop
+
+**Idea:** a capsule-lit corner and tall cobalt niche make the next turn recognisable.
+
+- **Kit:** existing Slab_*, Wall_Solid_4m/2m, cobalt variants, Partition_Glass_4m/2m and selected Window_4m/2m; 
proposed RoundedReturn_2x2, curved-glass return, capsule cove and low counter.
+- **Form:** niche **600 × 3,400**, end radius **300**, **recessed 60** in a 200 wall, leaving **140 skin**; silver 
**recessed 2**; sky print **recessed 20** above **2,600**; cove **recessed 80** in the slab, leaving **120 skin**; 
floor colour **flush 0**; cyan **10 wide**, **recessed 2**, filled flush.
+- **Materials:** gloss white/cobalt, polished resin, clear glass with high frost, inset silver and printed sky.
+- **Play:** **16 × 12 m section**, **4 m main route / 2 m open bypass**, reconnecting around the island; **4–8 m 
target exposed views**; **1.1 m counter** outside circulation; full-height returns stop the next sightline.
+- **Navigate/read:** **L / LEGAL capsule**, cobalt floor field and thin guide turning toward the hub; white backing 
preserves the glass-side enemy silhouette.
+
+### B — Offset planes
+
+**Idea:** staggered planes make the turn itself the landmark.
+
+- **Kit:** the same flat slabs/walls/partitions; proposed low block counter and flush L graphic; no curved-return 
mesh.
+- **Form:** stagger returns **2,000** on the grid; L/colour **flush 0**; silver **recessed 2**; ceiling slot 
**recessed 40**, leaving **160 slab skin**; cyan as A; no fins or raised letters.
+- **Materials:** glossy planar white/cobalt, resin, near-clear glass and separate high frost.
+- **Play:** shared loop and **2 m branch**, **4–8 m views**, **1.1 m counter** and full-height returns; offsets 
prevent a single uninterrupted tunnel.
+- **Navigate/read:** storey-height flush **L**, asymmetrical returns and an open branch; keep the enemy's slot 
against white.
+
+**Build A:** its capsule corner carries the era and the route without requiring small text.
+B supplies the cheaper flat-wall connector.
+
+## 02 · Junctions and doors
+
+[Sheet](02_Junctions_Doors/sheet_r5.png) · [Top-down](02_Junctions_Doors/layout_r5.png) · **1 image try**
+
+### A — Sky-lens T
+
+**Idea:** a high sky lens and unlike corner treatments distinguish the branches.
+
+- **Kit:** existing Wall_Door_4m, Door_Leaf, cobalt walls, partitions and slabs; proposed sky-lens finish, optional 
rounded return and capsule counter.
+- **Form:** sky insert **3,600 × 800**, above **2,800**, radius **400**, **recessed 40**, leaving **160 wall skin**; 
door reveal **recessed 15**; silver **recessed 2**; small corner finish **recessed at most 80**, retaining **120 
skin**; graphics **flush 0**.
+- **Materials:** white/cobalt gloss, sky print, polished resin, clear corner/high frost and silver door.
+- **Play:** **4 m T approach**, left/right branches, secondary **1.2 m door**; **4–8 m views**; **1.1 m counter** and 
full-height solid return.
+- **Navigate/read:** **R / REVIEW**, sky lens, cobalt left return and glass right corner; the door stays subordinate 
to the route.
+
+### B — Split X
+
+**Idea:** offset exits reveal short peeks instead of one four-way shooting tunnel.
+
+- **Kit:** existing 2 m/4 m walls, doors, partitions and slabs; proposed flush R graphic and low block; no special X 
mesh.
+- **Form:** offset opposite exits **2,000**; cove **recessed 40**, silver **recessed 2**, letter and colour **flush 
0**; ordinary door stays **1,200 × 2,400**.
+- **Materials:** gloss white/cobalt, pale resin, near-clear glass, high frost and quiet silver.
+- **Play:** **4 m approach / 2–4 m open branches**, reconnecting around wall islands; **4–8 m views**, **1.1 m 
cover**, full-height return cover.
+- **Navigate/read:** large flush **R**, one cobalt terminus, a clear corner and a ceiling line toward the next hub; 
white backs the opponent.
+
+**Build B:** it controls simultaneous angles with existing flat pieces.
+The sketch's dashed T cap is A's alternate termination; B opens that arm and staggers the returns.
+
+## 03 · Rooms and cover
+
+[Sheet](03_Rooms_Cover/sheet_r5.png) · [Top-down](03_Rooms_Cover/layout_r5.png) · **1 image try**
+
+### A — Capsule meeting room
+
+**Idea:** one solid capsule desk anchors a compact room loop.
+
+- **Kit:** existing wall/door/slab/flat partition modules; proposed Counter_Capsule_2m, high frosted capsule lintel 
and optional curved-glass corner; one simple chair outside circulation.
+- **Form:** counter **2,000 × 1,000 × 1,100 high**, end radius **500**, solid to the floor; top joint **recessed 2**, 
filled flush; high lintel at **2,100–2,500**, cut **recessed 30** inside 100 depth, leaving **70 skin**; sky print 
**recessed 20** above **2,600**; codes **flush 0**.
+- **Materials:** glossy white counter, cobalt rear plane, pale resin, clear glass/high frost and silver.
+- **Play:** **8 × 8 m room**, **2 m outer loop**, two **1.2 m doors** on adjacent sides; **4–8 m views**; **1.1 m 
crouch-cover target**, a **2 m-long full-height return**, and at least **2 m clear circulation** around the desk.
+- **Navigate/read:** **C / CLAIMS** high lintel and capsule silhouette; glass reveals the enemy beside the solid 
return, without office clutter.
+
+### B — Negative-space office
+
+**Idea:** reduce the room to one low monolith, one hard-cover return and a C.
+
+- **Kit:** same flat room shell; proposed Counter_Monolith_4m and flush C graphic.
+- **Form:** counter **4,000 × 1,000 × 1,100 high**; optional radius-**400**, maximum **250-deep inward scoop** on the 
non-combat end only; preserve the solid cover-facing body; top joint **recessed 2**, filled flush; code/colour **flush 
0**; frost above **2,100**.
+- **Materials:** gloss white/cobalt, polished resin and clear glass/high frost; no equipment or chairs.
+- **Play:** same **8 × 8 m room / 2 m outer loop / adjacent exits**, **4–8 m views**; the longer **1.1 m block** 
splits circulation while leaving both ends open; standing cover remains full-height.
+- **Navigate/read:** large flush **C**, asymmetrical cover and visible secondary door; white backs the glass-side 
figure.
+
+**Build A:** its shorter counter preserves circulation and a recognisable meeting-room cue.
+B's long counter is an alternative footprint, not an extra block beside A.
+
+## 04 · Atrium and vertical
+
+[Sheet](04_Atrium_Vertical/sheet_r5.png) · [Top-down](04_Atrium_Vertical/layout_r5.png) · **2 image tries**
+
+### A — Capsule spiral
+
+**Idea:** the retained spiral is an arrival landmark behind transparent balconies.
+
+- **Kit:** existing Stair_Flight, Stair_Steps, Stair_Column, Stair_CagePanel and stairwell slab where its hole fits; 
proposed capsule core finish, mezzanine-edge slabs, frameless guards and counters.
+- **Form:** core niche **1,000 × 3,000**, radius **500**, **recessed 120 radially** from radius **800** to **680**; 
silver **recessed 2**; cove **recessed 80**, leaving **120 slab skin**; H/landing field **flush 0**; remove opaque 
handrail tubes from the visual variant, retaining walking geometry and original radii/path.
+- **Materials:** white/cobalt gloss core, silver treads, near-clear curved cage/guards and polished resin; no 
projecting halo or opaque guard bars.
+- **Play:** **16 × 16 m double-height hub**, upper deck **4.5 m**, **8–12 m principal views** broken by piers; two 
lower flank routes reconnect; **1.1 m counters**; the spiral radial annulus is **1.8 m before edge clearances**, not a 
claimed 2 m-wide lane.
+- **Navigate/read:** **H / HEARINGS capsule**, visible treads, cobalt arrival field and upper return doors; clear 
guards preserve the enemy silhouette.
+
+### B — Folded forum
+
+**Idea:** broad stair, terraces, short ramp and drop give the hub quick reconnects.
+
+- **Kit:** existing plain/cobalt walls and slabs; proposed Stair_Straight_2m in a **4 × 8 m bay**, mezzanine-edge 
slabs, frameless guards, Ramp_2x4, low shelf and block cover.
+- **Form:** proposed stair clear width **2,000**, rise **4,500**; **24 risers × 187.5** and **300 goings** are a 
modelling starting point, with remaining run reserved for connections/landings; resolve final flight fit in module 
drawings.
+- **Form continued:** ramp **2,000 wide × 4,000 horizontal run**, rise **1,000**, slope **1:4**, to a shelf with one 
open drop edge; graphics **flush 0**, slot **recessed 40**, guard fixings recessed within new slab-edge bounds and 
below **350 above the local deck**.
+- **Materials:** glossy white/cobalt planes, resin, almost-clear stair/balcony guards and inset silver; no opaque 
horizontal/diagonal handrail tubes.
+- **Play:** **16 × 16 m hub**, upper deck **4.5 m**, **8–12 m views**, full-height piers and **1.1 m cover**; **2 m 
stair** reaches the upper loop; ramp and **1 m drop** make a separate lower reconnect; upper routes rejoin the 
labyrinth.
+- **Navigate/read:** high cobalt open-square/**H** graphic, visible stair silhouette and thin ramp guide.
+- **Boundary:** slope locomotion, drop collision, flight fit and any fall-damage rule are proposals, not validated or 
decided by the artwork.
+
+**Build B:** the wide direct stair is the stronger main fast link.
+A remains the existing-kit alternative or secondary authored landmark.
+The sketch overlays A's circle and B's stair bay as alternatives, not a requirement to build both.
+
+## 05 · Glass walls
+
+[Sheet](05_Glass_Walls/sheet_r5.png) · [Top-down](05_Glass_Walls/layout_r5.png) · **1 image try**
+
+### A — Skyglass suite
+
+**Idea:** high frosted capsules name the room above almost-clear combat panes.
+
+- **Kit:** existing flat partitions, solid/cobalt walls, slabs and doors; proposed high frosted inserts, optional 
curved return and break-ready **2 m pane module**.
+- **Form:** high capsule **3,000 × 300**, wholly within **2,100–2,500**, face **recessed 30** in 100-deep header; 
silver **recessed 2**; low frost stops at **350**; pane stays at its original plane; marks **flush 0**; cleared gap 
has no raised threshold or base rail.
+- **Materials:** near-clear two-streak glass, separate high/low frost, gloss white/cobalt, resin and silver.
+- **Play:** **12 × 12 m section**, **2 m bypass**, **4–8 m views**, **1.1 m counter** and full-height returns; two 
panes reveal threats; depicted **2 m cleared break opening** joins the bypass.
+- **Navigate/read:** **A / ARCHIVE** lintel and cobalt terminus; faint sheen/edge means intact pane, absence of 
pane/foot rail means opened route; fragments indicate state, not a debris implementation.
+
+### B — Transparency cuts
+
+**Idea:** solid, visible-but-closed and visible-open cells form a simple combat alphabet.
+
+- **Kit:** existing 2 m/4 m walls, partitions and slabs; proposed high frosted strip, low block and break-ready pane 
variant; no complicated special wall mesh.
+- **Form:** alternate **2,000-wide cells**; solid **4,300 high**, partition **2,500 high**, frost **2,100–2,500 / 
0–350**; silver **recessed 2**, slot **recessed 40**, A/colour **flush 0**; no body-height frost or crossbar.
+- **Materials:** the same clear/frosted/solid distinction as A, using planar white/cobalt and resin without a capsule 
lens.
+- **Play:** **12 × 12 m section**, **2 m bypass**, **4–8 m views**, **1.1 m block** and full-height returns; a 
cleared pane opens a flank that rejoins an already viable loop.
+- **Navigate/read:** giant flush terminal **A**, staggered piers and distinct closed/open cells; white enemy backing 
and a two-pane visibility target.
+
+**Build B:** alternating simple bays explain the route states most clearly.
+Use A's lintel selectively for departmental identity.
+
+## Existing kit items to reconsider
+
+These are handoff flags, not changes made to the kit.
+
+| Existing item/assumption | Labyrinth handoff |
+| --- | --- |
+| Rival façade, street trays, three-floor exterior composition | Selected outer window routes replace the mandatory 
street read; exterior detailing no longer leads this kit. |
+| Carpet/tiled-ceiling source language | Unity's floor is already polished, but the kit README/source texture 
workflow still describe carpet and ceiling tiles; retain polished mapping and propose flat coved ceilings. |
+| One portal/floor index per tower floor | Zones need distinct landmarks; L/R/C/H/A are proposed department 
identities, not a new global numbering rule. |
+| Frame-wide partition collider | The source builder places collision over the whole partition on its frame; the 
shooting lane must coordinate pane, frame/threshold and collision removal for a walkable break opening. |
+| Fixed stair cage/silver handrail | The colliding cage and opaque rail need review for transparent combat guards; 
this pass does not decide destructibility or collision policy. |
+| Full-height locked red stair leaf | It belongs to earlier progression gating and can obstruct fast loops; this pass 
neither assumes it on every combat stair nor removes its game rule. |
+| Spiral as sole vertical link | The 1.8 m radial annulus is less direct than the proposed main stair; wide stairs, 
mezzanine edges, ramp and drop remain proposed modules. |
+| 600-high window sill | Keep at outer windows; it is below the requested 1.0–1.2 m crouch-cover range and cannot be 
the sole interior cover piece. |
+| No dedicated clean low-cover family | 1.1 m capsule/block counters need explicit meshes/colliders; open-legged 
desks do not provide the painted cover. |
+| Baked floor reflections | Moving figures are omitted currently; painted figure reflections are a target, not an 
implemented effect/performance claim. |
+
+The kit README's tower layout/projectile assumptions are older than FEEDBACK_05.
+**FEEDBACK_05 is authoritative for these concepts**; projectile interaction stays with the shooting lane.
+No gameplay, model, prefab, collider, material, shader or netcode implementation was changed.
+No system setup changes were made, and the write-only-here instruction excludes updates to boards/system docs 
elsewhere.
+
